---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy policy | European Scrap Market"
  description="How European Scrap Market handles your data in accordance with GDPR."
>

<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-8">
  <p class="mono" data-reveal>LEGAL</p>
  <h1 class="display h-section mt-3" data-reveal>Privacy <span class="grad-text">policy</span></h1>

  <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-muted)]" data-reveal>
    <p>European Scrap Market processes personal data in accordance with the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).</p>

    <h2 class="display text-lg font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)]">What we collect</h2>
    <p>When you submit a scrap request: your name, email, phone (optional), country, and the details you provide about your scrap. When you become a partner: company details and verification documents.</p>

    <h2 class="display text-lg font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)]">How we use it</h2>
    <p>To connect you with a verified scrap yard in your country, to verify partners, and to provide the marketplace service. We do not sell your data.</p>

    <h2 class="display text-lg font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Who sees your data</h2>
    <p>Before a yard takes your case, it sees only material, weight, and country. Once a yard accepts your case, it gets your contact details — only that yard, never several at once, and never publicly.</p>

    <h2 class="display text-lg font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Your rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right to access, correct, and delete your data. Contact support@europeanscrapmarket.com to exercise these rights.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-amber-800" data-reveal>
    <strong>Placeholder:</strong> This is a draft privacy policy. Final text should be reviewed by a qualified lawyer before going live.
  </div>
</div>

</Layout>
